<title>AUSTRIA: Creditanstalt bidders fail - agency.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt bidders fail - agency.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium of bidders for privatisation candidate Creditanstalt appeared to have failed to agree on an offer for the bank, Austrian newsagency APA said on Friday.</p>
<p>A group of bidders around savings bank Die Erste and insurer EA-Generali was given until midnight Friday to submit a final offer for the flagship bank.  </p>
<p>Independent confirmation for the report was not immediately available.</p>
<p>APA said EA-Generali was now likely to turn to other members of the consortium, which include Banca Commerciale Italiana, Germany's Commerzbank and several Austrian companies to work on a new offer for the government's 70 percent voting stake in Creditanstalt.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Viktor Klima has said he will reopen the six-year long privatisation process to other parties on Monday if the consortium fails to agree on a bid by midnight Friday.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
